WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:05.290
Welcome to R&D Tax Workbench UK! In this walkthrough, we'll prepare a complete UK R&D

00:05.290 --> 00:09.980
claim under the merged R&D expenditure credit scheme for Fernhill Robotics, from sign-up

00:09.980 --> 00:14.670
to the additional information form and the CT600 boxes. Let's dive in!

00:16.700 --> 00:21.650
Getting started takes seconds. Create an account with your name, your email and a password.

00:22.050 --> 00:24.210
Confirm the password, and you're in.

00:28.500 --> 00:32.500
The AI features, like narratives and account classification, run on credits. Open the

00:32.500 --> 00:36.500
credit meter, choose a top-up, and pay securely through Stripe.

00:38.533 --> 00:41.873
Business details are needed once, before your first top-up.

00:43.833 --> 00:46.373
Pay by card through Stripe's secure checkout.

00:49.133 --> 00:51.213
Add the billing address, and pay.

00:53.233 --> 00:57.103
Payment confirmed, and the credits land in your balance straight away.

01:00.266 --> 01:04.386
Create a new claim. Enter the company name, its tax reference and SIC code.

01:06.186 --> 01:09.881
Then the accounting period. It starts after 1 April 2024, so the merged R&D expenditure

01:09.881 --> 01:13.576
credit scheme applies.

01:13.976 --> 01:17.926
Answer a few questions on company size and status, and create the claim.

01:19.899 --> 01:24.499
Claim settings hold the figures the computation needs, starting with the company's status.

01:24.899 --> 01:27.969
Then the corporation tax figures before R&D relief.

01:28.369 --> 01:32.649
And the PAYE and National Insurance figures, for the cap on the payable credit.

01:33.049 --> 01:35.769
Add the contacts for the additional information form.

01:42.009 --> 01:45.179
The company made an R&D claim in the last three years, so it doesn't need to tell HMRC

01:45.179 --> 01:48.349
in advance that it plans to claim.

01:50.366 --> 01:56.606
The company page keeps the details together, with the claim time limit: 31 March 2028.

01:58.599 --> 02:01.259
Now the R&D project. Paste in your own notes, and the AI project setup drafts the project

02:01.259 --> 02:03.919
for you.

02:09.905 --> 02:13.120
It proposes the R&D activities and the directly contributing activity, in the terms the

02:13.120 --> 02:16.335
government's guidelines use.

02:16.735 --> 02:20.795
Create the project, and the narrative for every activity is written in one go.

02:22.151 --> 02:25.831
Every activity now has its full narrative, ready to review and edit.

02:36.097 --> 02:39.497
Payroll next. Upload the payroll file, and AI maps the columns: gross pay, employer National

02:39.497 --> 02:42.897
Insurance and employer pension.

02:43.297 --> 02:46.777
A quick quality check, then import. Seven employees are loaded.

02:50.097 --> 02:52.912
Now the timesheet. The smart parser reads each person's R&D hours and matches them to

02:52.912 --> 02:55.727
the activities.

02:57.237 --> 02:59.247
Review the mappings, and save.

03:01.937 --> 03:05.377
The combined view brings it together: each person's salary, National Insurance and pension,

03:05.377 --> 03:08.817
apportioned by actual R&D hours.

03:10.663 --> 03:13.318
Now the financials. Upload the general ledger. The parser reads every account and checks

03:13.318 --> 03:15.973
the file.

03:16.923 --> 03:20.553
24 accounts, parsed and checked. Import them, and AI classifies each one against the UK

03:20.553 --> 03:24.183
rules, with a reason for every decision.

03:24.583 --> 03:27.608
Salaries, contractors, materials, cloud and data costs are picked out as R&D, and loan

03:27.608 --> 03:30.633
interest is excluded.

03:34.823 --> 03:39.453
Upload the trial balance separately. Each source is stored and reconciled on its own.

03:46.138 --> 03:49.178
Then the profit and loss statement and the balance sheet.

03:51.998 --> 03:56.658
The ledger is an expense-only extract, so mark it as partial, and the sources reconcile.

03:59.478 --> 04:04.408
Review the profit and loss items marked as R&D. A category can be changed with one click.

04:12.392 --> 04:16.882
Apportionment. Choose a just and reasonable basis for each cost, and record why. Staff

04:16.882 --> 04:21.372
costs follow the timesheets, including employer National Insurance and pension.

04:32.752 --> 04:37.782
Cloud computing, contractors and materials are wholly for R&D, so they're allocated directly.

04:38.182 --> 04:43.102
The design software is shared across engineering, so it uses the R&D share of staff time.

04:44.582 --> 04:47.972
The test facility's power is metered separately, so it's allocated directly too. Every

04:47.972 --> 04:51.362
choice has a note, ready if HMRC asks.

04:55.862 --> 04:59.892
And the comparison shows how the choice of method changes the R&D spend.

05:01.892 --> 05:04.872
Contractors. Record each one as externally provided workers or subcontracted R&D, so the

05:04.872 --> 05:07.852
UK rules apply.

05:08.252 --> 05:11.302
Avonbridge University's robotics lab modelled the soil and tine interaction. It's an unconnected

05:11.302 --> 05:14.352
subcontractor.

05:18.592 --> 05:25.382
Unconnected subcontractors count at 65% of the payment, so £80,000 gives £52,000.

05:25.782 --> 05:29.062
Brightwork supplied two agency test engineers on UK payroll: externally provided workers,

05:29.062 --> 05:32.342
also at 65%.

05:42.622 --> 05:46.226
Delft Field Robotics ran trials in the Netherlands because it was convenient. Overseas

05:46.226 --> 05:49.829
work only counts when conditions in the UK can't support it, and cost or convenience doesn't

05:49.829 --> 05:53.432
count, so it's excluded.

06:06.782 --> 06:10.892
Link each contractor to the activities it worked on, as evidence for the claim.

06:33.462 --> 06:37.482
Each card shows the R&D share, and the qualifying amount after the rules.

06:48.292 --> 06:51.732
Other expenses: consumables, software, data licences and cloud computing. AI has already

06:51.732 --> 06:55.172
picked out the five R&D accounts.

06:57.532 --> 07:00.959
In claim settings, confirm the UK cost category for each account. The crop image library

07:00.959 --> 07:04.386
is a data licence, the GPU training is cloud computing, and the test facility's power

07:04.386 --> 07:07.812
is a consumable.

07:08.212 --> 07:10.967
The R&D intensity test for ERIS uses the total expenditure in the accounts. One click

07:10.967 --> 07:13.722
fills it in.

07:14.122 --> 07:16.182
And add the date the claim will be made.

07:25.025 --> 07:29.235
The summary. Every cost is grouped by category at its qualifying amount, under the merged

07:29.235 --> 07:33.445
scheme. The one warning confirms the overseas trials are excluded.

07:33.845 --> 07:41.435
Qualifying expenditure is £580,000, so the expenditure credit at 20% is £116,000.

07:41.835 --> 07:47.035
The seven statutory steps follow the CT600L boxes. The credit first pays this year's corporation

07:47.035 --> 07:52.235
tax, and after the notional tax step, £14,700 is payable.

07:52.635 --> 07:56.175
The company is exempt from the PAYE cap, and the claim is in time.

08:01.715 --> 08:06.245
Any point the law can read more than one way is listed as a position for you to decide.

08:08.192 --> 08:12.277
Before the outputs, the additional information form needs each project's answers. AI drafts

08:12.277 --> 08:16.362
them from your notes and narratives, without adding facts.

08:16.762 --> 08:19.167
Anything it can't find is left as a question for you, so review each answer and make it

08:19.167 --> 08:21.572
yours.

08:25.902 --> 08:28.562
Outputs. The additional information form draft is complete, with no errors and nothing

08:28.562 --> 08:31.222
missing.

08:31.622 --> 08:34.352
Business details, contacts, the expenditure credit figures by category, and each project's

08:34.352 --> 08:37.082
answers.

08:46.102 --> 08:50.582
Then every CT600 and CT600L box, ready to copy into the return.

08:53.202 --> 08:57.242
Download the computation workpaper in Excel, and the answers as plain text.

09:02.759 --> 09:08.034
That's a complete UK R&D claim, from ledgers and timesheets to the additional information

09:08.034 --> 09:13.309
form and the CT600 boxes. Thanks so much for watching, and find out more at rdinnovate.com.
